 "about": "Tin Hat games v1.1 economy rules (GAMES-V1.1-ADDENDUM §5.2, §6.2, §6.3), as pure cases for the server (games-s2 writes, games-design2 reviews). vectors/ledger.json is unchanged and keeps running with the v1 defaults (rules.V1_DEFAULTS); these cases use the v1.1 defaults unless a case gives `server` (the server-wide env values) and `space` (the space's own settings). Sections: `economy` = the resolved value + source per key (economyFor over configFromEnv); `tick` = sampler samples at the resolved economy (rules.tick; w = {holdings, rank, accrual_s, day, earned_today}, ev = {at, gap_s, eligible}); `admin_delta` = the chips one admin action moves for one wallet (+ mints from mint:admin, − burns to burn:admin; open money is refused before this for everything but a grant); `side_pay` = Tune In's pay on a find; `side_tombstone` = what a deleted-and-rejoined wallet's side counters are. The DB-level rules (all-or-nothing named lists, the op receipt, the log, notices, exactly-once side pay) are tested in the server's test/play-r2-admin.test.mjs and test/play-r2-side.test.mjs.",
